47:Floor material per room (laid by the part that builds the shell): foyer checker `quartz_block`/`black_concrete` (cell (x+z) even = quartz); office, dining `dark_oak_planks`; kitchen, family, bay nook, passages, gallery, BR2-4, primary, closet `oak_planks`; bath `smooth_quartz`; garage `light_gray_concrete`; mudroom `stone_bricks`; bonus `spruce_planks`. The y=5 slab layer carries the upper room floors; the same layer is the ceiling under them.
50:- `wallBlock(face,x,y,z)`: y=0 `stone_bricks`; y5 and y9 on exterior planes `smooth_quartz`; north-facing wall plane (see PALETTE) y1..4 veneer hash; else `birch_planks`. `quoins`: at corner columns (1,7),(17,7),(18,11),(1,24),(17,24),(18,25),(35,25),(42,24): corner cell y1..9 `quartz_block`; the neighbour cell along each exposed face is `quartz_block` when y is even, siding when odd (skip y=5, y=9 which are already bands). `shutterCells`: for every window in OPENINGS flagged `sh`, wall cells at x0-1 and x1+1 (or z0-1, z1+1 on x-faces) over the window's y-range are `black_concrete`.
51:- `archWindow(x0,x1,yb,yt,plane,face)` (P4): fill the opening with `glass_pane`; top row corner cells x0 and x1 at yt become `quartz_stairs` half=top, facing = away from the window centre (x0: west, x1: east) so they read as arch springers; if the window is 1 wide put `quartz_slab` type=top at yt instead of a pane; sill = row of `quartz_slab` type=top on the outside plane (plane-1 for north faces) at y=yb-1 across x0..x1; hood = row of `quartz_slab` type=bottom on the outside plane at y=yt+1.
52:- `entryDoor` (P4): opening x25..28 y1..4 at z=11. `dark_oak_door` at x26 and x27, y1..2 (lower+upper half), facing north, hinges on the outer ends so the pair meets in the middle (check `mcd states dark_oak_door` and a render), sidelights `glass_pane` x25 and x28 y1..3, transom row y=3 x26,x27 `glass_pane`, fan row y=4 x26,x27 `glass_pane`, springers `quartz_stairs` half=top at (25,4) facing west and (28,4) facing east. Palladian window above: opening x25..28 y6..8 at z=11: `glass_pane` fill, springers `quartz_stairs` half=top at (25,8) facing west and (28,8) facing east, sill and hood as `archWindow`.
